// command.json: send commands to the scan engine while a run is going.
// The engine reads this file every few seconds and applies each new command.
//
// How to send a command:
//   - Add an entry to "commands" and save the file. Write the whole file at once
//     (write a temporary file, then rename it over this one).
//   - "seq" must be higher than every earlier command for this run and is never reused.
//     The engine applies only commands with a seq above the last one it has seen.
//   - "runId" must match the run, or the engine ignores the file.
//   - "id", "issuedAt" (UTC, ISO-8601) and "issuedBy" are for the record.
//   - Leave earlier commands in the file. Ones already applied are skipped.
//   - Lines starting with // are comments and are allowed.
//
// Supported commands ("type", then its "args"):
//   Pause           Finish repos in progress, start no new ones, and hold.
//                   args: none
//   Resume          Continue after a Pause.
//                   args: none
//   Stop            Finish repos in progress, then end the run as Stopped.
//                   args: none
//   Abort           Stop now: kill running tools and end the run as Stopped.
//                   args: none
//   SetConcurrency  Change how many repos a tool works on at once.
//                   args: tool (a tool name, or "all"), maxParallel (a whole number, 1 to 256)
//   DisableTool     Start no new work for a tool.
//                   args: tool, reason (optional)
//   RetryFailed     Requeue the repos that failed in this run.
//                   args: tool (optional, leave out for every tool)
//   SkipRepo        Drop one repo from all the work that remains.
//                   args: repoKey, for example "gh-91234"
//
// Tool names: Rapid7, CheckMarx, RepoClone, TruffleHog, Semgrep, Snyk, SonarStandard, SonarDotNet
//
// Example entry:
//   { "seq": 1, "id": "b7e1-0001", "type": "SetConcurrency", "issuedAt": "2026-10-14T04:30:00Z",
//     "issuedBy": "phil", "args": { "tool": "TruffleHog", "maxParallel": 3 } }
//
// The outcome of each command (Applied, Rejected or Ignored) is shown in status.json under "commandAcks".
{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "runId": "2026-10-10T23-38-46Z",
  "commands": []
}